# Copy to .env for local development.
#
# Both values come from Supabase › Project Settings › API. The anon key is a
# public client key: it is compiled into the JS bundle and anyone can read it.
# That is fine — Row-Level Security is the actual boundary, and the anon key on
# its own grants nothing until a user signs in. Never put the service_role key
# here; it belongs only in the edge function's environment.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
